-- title:
--   The q+1 ends of the blown-up supersingular chart
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$, and a positive integer $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, let $\xi\in L$ be a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that some ring homomorphism $\iota\colon L\to\mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which (`hK`) is the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_H$ with $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ and $H=\ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times\bigr)$, i.e. $K=\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,L\,(\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,N_0\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell)\,M'))$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring which is a domain with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ in the image of $A$ (`hξA`), and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L\subseteq K$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant (`hj`), let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C=\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and let $y\subset C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense (`hss`) that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (a Drinfeld-chart rigidification at all supersingular points of the special fibre, summarised here) requires: for every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X=\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$ (the pushout of $\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ and the chart attached to $j^{-1}$ along the middle chart) at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ mapping to $z$ whose prime satisfies the same supersingularity condition as $y$, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a homomorphism $\sigma\colon A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv \mathrm{drinfeldForm}\,q\,W=X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e\colon \widehat{\mathcal O}_{\mathfrak X,z}\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;S:=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(\mathrm{C}(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v-fu\bigr)$$
--   from the adic completion of the stalk, subject to seven riders: $e$ carries the germ of each $a\in A$ to the class of $\mathrm{C}(\sigma a)$; every automorphism $\tau$ of $K/L$ implementing $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserves $C$; for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ such a $\tau$ is the identity on $C/y'$; each such $\tau$ which is the identity on $C/y'$ is induced by an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ fixing constants whose linear part is a matrix $M$ over $W$ with $M\equiv c\gamma$, $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, with $c\equiv 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ and $c\not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; two primes of $S$ through the origin of the special fibre with tangent directions $(a_1,b_1)$, $(a_2,b_2)$ satisfying $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$ have distinct contractions to the stalk; a prime of $S$ with tangent direction $(1,0)$ contracts to the set of those $a\in C$ all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $\mathfrak m_A\cdot A$; and the element of $C$ given by $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,L\,(q\ell)$, corrected by a constant $a_0\in A$ so as to lie in $y'$, corresponds under $e$ to a series $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e_0\ge 1$ whose degree-$e_0$ leading form is a unit at every $W$-point $(a,b)$, not both non-units, with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$ (a Hasse-invariant rider). Here `IsLevelAutAt` expresses that $\tau$ acts on $K$ as substitution by $\gamma^{-1}$: it compares, through the complex reading $\iota$ of $\xi$, the $q$-expansion of $\tau x$ for $x$ a ratio of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ with the expansions of those forms pulled back along $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$.
--
--   Fixed in addition are: the point $z$ with its germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ in the maximal ideal of the stalk, a point $y'$ of $\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ above $z$ satisfying the supersingularity condition (`hss'`), with $y'$ the prime $y$ (`hy'y`); and one chart witness at $z$: a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, $\sigma_1\colon A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$, units $u_1,v_1$, a series $f_1$ congruent to $\mathrm{drinfeldForm}\,q\,W_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ of $\widehat{\mathcal O}_{\mathfrak X,z}$ with $S=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(\mathrm{C}(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1)$, together with the hypothesis `hW₁` asserting for this witness the same seven riders as listed above.
--
--   Further data: an ideal $J\subseteq C$ which (`hJ`) is the infimum, i.e. the intersection, of the ideals obtained as follows: for $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, take the contraction along $e_1\circ(\text{completion})\circ(\text{germ at }z)$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $\mathrm{C}(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$, $X_1$, and pull it back along the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$. An $A$-subalgebra $B\subseteq K$ which (`hB`) equals the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x\in K:\ x\varpi_t\in J\}$, that is $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$. A valuation subring $W\subseteq K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`).
--
--   The remaining hypotheses are: `hR1`, that $C\subseteq B$ and $K$ is the field of fractions of $B$; `hR2`, that $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that $W$ meets $L$ exactly in $A$, that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak m_W$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak m_W$ (every $f\in W$ is $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\notin\mathfrak m_W$, and conversely); and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here), that for each $(\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2)$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho\colon B\to\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,k$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring with kernel $B\cap\mathfrak m_W$, extending $A\to k$, and equivariant for every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, preserving $W$, via an element $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ of $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ acting through $\mathrm{hAction}$, with $c\neq1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\neq\mathrm{id}$; that $B$ is stable under all such $\tau$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ contains the image of $B\cap\mathfrak m_W$ under some level automorphism with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ carried into $\mathfrak m_W$ by all such automorphisms is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and that a level automorphism with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$. Finally, $\gamma_0\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau_0$ a level automorphism at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ with $W$ stable under $\tau_0$ (`hτ₀W`).
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exists a finite set $\mathrm{ends}$ of subrings $O$ of $K$ with the following five properties.
--
--   First, a subring $O\subseteq K$ belongs to $\mathrm{ends}$ if and only if there is a nonzero $a\in J\subseteq C$ such that, setting $B_a$ to be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ generated over $C$ by $\{x\in K:\ \exists\,i\in J,\ xa=i\}$, i.e. $B_a=C[J/a]$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ for which: $O$ is the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$, in the sense that $f\in O$ precisely when $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_a$ and $h\notin P$; every element of $y$ which lies in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$; and $B$ is not contained in $O$.
--
--   Second, the cardinality of $\mathrm{ends}$ is $q+1$.
--
--   Third, $\mathrm{ends}$ is permuted by the level automorphisms preserving $W$: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $f\in W\iff\tau f\in W$, each $O\in\mathrm{ends}$ admits an $O'\in\mathrm{ends}$ with $f\in O\iff\tau f\in O'$ for all $f\in K$.
--
--   Fourth, this action is transitive: for any $O,O'\in\mathrm{ends}$ there are $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ such that $W$ is stable under $\tau$ and $f\in O\iff\tau f\in O'$ for all $f\in K$.
--
--   Fifth, $\tau_0$ fixes every end: $f\in O\iff\tau_0 f\in O$ for all $O\in\mathrm{ends}$ and all $f\in K$.
--
--   Sixth, distinct ends are separated: if $O\neq O'$ in $\mathrm{ends}$, there is an $f\in K$ lying in both $O$ and $O'$ which is a non-unit of $O$ and a unit of $O'$.
--
--   This is the step that identifies, at a supersingular point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of the level-$\Gamma_H$ modular curve, the $q+1$ ends of the blow-up along the weighted centre $J$: they are the local rings of the charts $C[J/a]$ at maximal ideals not dominating $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$, and they correspond to the $q+1$ tangent directions over $\mathbb F_q$ of the Drinfeld form $X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$, on which the level automorphisms act transitively while $\tau_0$ fixes each. It feeds the assembly of the cyclic decomposition of the ends together with the Hasse and Igusa data over the common chart cover of the blow-up.
